 applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals of Speculation: Might", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We can use certain <strong>modal verbs</strong> to make assumptions or speculations about something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In English language, we can use <b>modal verbs</b> to express necessity, obligation, probability and <b>speculation</b>, among others. In this learning point, we are going to talk about <b>modal verbs</b> that indicate<b> speculation</b>. We can speculate about a situation when we consider or believe something is, was, or is going to take place in a certain way.<br/><br/>   Some common <b>modal verbs</b> we can use to speculate are: Can, could, may and <strong>might.</strong><br/><br/>  To use a modal to make a <b>speculation</b> you only have to follow this structure:<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <b>modal verb</b>+ <b>main verb</b> + complement</div><br/><br/>  Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">It <strong>might be</strong> better to learn how the \u2018if statements' work first.<br/> It <strong>might have been</strong> easier to start with the simple form of \u2018if statements'.<br/> We <strong>might be reviewing</strong> \u2018if statements' next session.</span><br/><br/>  Note that we can use <b>modal verbs</b> with different tenses depending on what we want to express. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It <strong>might come</strong> in handy to read the magazine. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <strong>might be</strong> familiar with the conditional statements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It <strong>might sound</strong> difficult, but if you write the code neatly, you won't have any trouble.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Flowchart of How the If Else Statement Works", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <strong>if-else</strong> statements in JavaScript help people build results based on controlled conditions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "To understand the basics of how the conditional statements in JavaScript work, take a look at the following chart. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05img01.jpg", "type": "image"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hi-tech ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "referring to high technology ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: I've been reading this hi-tech magazine that made a review on JavaScript for beginners.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "come in handy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something useful that might be perfect for a situation ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It might come in handy to read the magazine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "neatly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "done in a very careful, organized and clean way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It might sound difficult, but if you write the code neatly, you won't have any trouble.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rely on ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to trust someone or something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The basic control statement which JavaScript relies on to make decisions.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "level-up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the next level or the improved version of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The last is the \"if...else...if\" statement: it's the level-up of the \"if...else\" statements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "try something out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to use something, usually for the first time, to see if it works", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'll have to try it out to see if I can get the output right.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for more information about conditional statements on JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a brochure where you define the statements and provide examples.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a presentation about one of the conditional statements. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your presentation with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I understand what conditional statements on JavaScript are.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I list the conditional statements. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the characteristics of conditional statements. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}]}